msgid "Hide"
msgstr "Steek weg"

#: rc.cpp:57
msgid "Show"
msgstr "Vertoon"

#: rc.cpp:58
msgid "Action for this filter"
msgstr "Aksie vir hierdie filter"

#: rc.cpp:59
msgid ""
"Here you can define what should happen if this filter matches (e.g. whether "
"the matching articles should be shown or hidden)."
msgstr ""
"Hier jy kan definieer wat moet gebeur as hierdie filter ooreenstemmende "
"inskrywings (e.g. hetsy die ooreenstemmende aktikels moet wees vertoon of "
"weg gesteekte)."

#: rc.cpp:60
msgid "articles from"
msgstr "aktikels van"

#: rc.cpp:62
msgid "Affected news sources"
msgstr "Geaffekteer nuus bronkodes"

#: rc.cpp:63
msgid ""
"Here you can specify which news sources (or all of them) are affected. Note "
"that only the news sources which have been activated on the <i>News "
"sources</i> tab are shown in this combo box."
msgstr ""
"Hier jy kan spesifiseer wat nuus bronkodes (van alle van hulle) word "
"geaffekteer. Nota wat slegs die nuus bronkodes wat het al geaktiveer op die "
"<i>nuus bronkodes</i> oortjie word vertoon in hierdie gekombineerde boks."

#: rc.cpp:64
msgid "whose"
msgstr "wie se"

#: rc.cpp:65
msgid "Keyword/Expression"
msgstr "Sleutelwoord/Uitdrukking"

#: rc.cpp:66
msgid ""
"Here you can type a keyword or expression which should be used for this "
"filter which depends on the condition you selected in the combo box at the "
"right:<ul>\n"
"<li><b>contain</b>, <b>doesn't contain</b> - you should probably enter a "
"keyword here, like \"KDE\", \"Baseball\" or \"Business\". The keyword is not "
"case-sensitive so it doesn't matter whether you type \"kde\", \"KDE\" or "
"\"kDe\".</li>\n"
"<li><b>equals</b>, <b>doesn't equal</b> - enter a phrase or expression here "
"to have the filter match only those articles whose headlines match "
"<b>exactly</b>"
" the text you typed. The phrase you type will be considered to be "
"case-sensitive, so it makes a difference whether you show articles which "
"contain \"Boeing\" or \"BOEING\".</li>\n"
"<li><b>matches</b> - a regular expression is expected. Recommended only if "
"you are familiar with regular expressions, i.e. it should be used by "
"advanced users only.</li></ul>"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:67
msgid "headlines"
msgstr "hoof opskrifte"

#: rc.cpp:68
msgid "contain"
msgstr "bevat"

#: rc.cpp:69
msgid "don't contain"
msgstr "moet nie bevat"

#: rc.cpp:70
msgid "equal"
msgstr "gelyk"

#: rc.cpp:71
msgid "don't equal"
msgstr "moet nie gelyk"

#: rc.cpp:72
msgid "match"
msgstr "ooreenstem"

#: rc.cpp:73
msgid "Condition for this filter"
msgstr "Kondisie vir hierdie filter"

#: rc.cpp:74
msgid ""
"This combo box lets you specify the condition under which the "
"keyword/expression you entered in the input field at the right will match. "
"You can select one of the following values:<ul>\n"
"<li>contain - the filter matches if the headline contains the keyword.</li>\n"
"<li>doesn't contain - the filter matches if the headline does not contain "
"the keyword.</li>\n"
"<li>equals - the filter matches if the headline equals the expression.</li>\n"
"<li>doesn't equal - the filter matches if the headline does not equal the "
"expression.</li>\n"
"<li>"
"matches - the filter matches if the expression matches the headline. The "
"expression you typed at the right will be considered a regular expression in "
"this mode.</li>"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:75
msgid "Scroller Preferences"
msgstr "Roller Voorkeure"

#: rc.cpp:76
msgid "Behavior"
msgstr "Gedrag"

#: rc.cpp:77
msgid "&Scrolling speed:"
